diff --git a/docs/recommendation-protocol.md b/docs/recommendation-protocol.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..bf676d3a89af8a809061e515d2719ad3fdd18cef
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/recommendation-protocol.md
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# Recommendation protocol v1
+
+The host owns authentication, Firestore reads, data loading and ranking. Godot renders a native interface. Credentials and UID never cross this protocol.
+
+Every command has `requestId` (1–64 ASCII letters/digits/underscore/hyphen), `sessionGeneration` (nonnegative safe integer), and `action`. Every response has `channel: "starpath-recommendations"`, `version: 1`, the same requestId/sessionGeneration and `type`. Each encoded message is at most 65536 UTF-8 bytes; list pages contain at most 20 rows. Exact field allowlists reject unknown fields.
+
+## Shared input
+
+`settings` is a complete object:
+
+```json
+{"source":"activeReport","manual":[],"examId":"","mode":"balanced","year":"115","applicantGender":"","filters":{"keyword":"","category":"","status":"all"}}
+```
+
+- source: `activeReport` or `manual`; manual rows: `{groupId,category,level:2|1}` (max 128, category required; level 2 means priority, 1 means also interested). Manual selection never changes the saved report. An empty manual list is valid for opening saved favorites: query returns zero recommendations and a choose-interests warning, while detail remains available for comparison.
+- examId: saved exam ID or empty string for exploration. mode: `balanced`, `interest`, `academic`. year: `115` (candidate year fixed; 113/114 are detail history only). applicantGender: empty, `male`, `female`, only used for an official gender-specific screening row.
+- filters: keyword (max 80), category (exact canonical major name or empty), status: `all`, `passed`, `failed`, `pending`, `explore`, `extension`.
+- Ranking points are internal only: I=2 best/priority, I=1 suitable/also interested; A=2 complete historical pass, A=1 complete historical fail; integer weights 5:5, 7:3, 3:7. Equal points share priorityTier, then programRef orders display only. No Z, prestige, number of matches or boost tiebreak. Pending/explore/extension have null priorityTier.
+
+## Commands and responses
+
+| action | additional command fields | response type and payload |
+|---|---|---|
+| bootstrap | none | `bootstrap`: `{settings,settingsRevision,activeReport:null|{recordId,revision,selectionRevision,title},catalog:[{groupId,groupLabel,category}],years:["115"],algorithmVersion,dataVersion}` |
+| listExams | `cursor:null|string` | `exams`: `{items:[{id,title,examDate,kind,summary,updatedAtMillis}],nextCursor:null|string}` |
+| query | `settings` | `results`: `{queryId,items, nextCursor:null|string,total,counts:{passed,failed,pending,explore,extension},inputs,warnings:[string]}` |
+| page | `queryId,cursor:string` | `results`: same shape as query, from the same immutable result snapshot |
+| detail | `queryId,programRef` | `detail`: `{queryId,item,details:{matchReasons:[string],academicStatus,missing:[string],rules:[{label,actual,required,passed}],boostPlans:[{summary,changes:[{subject,from,to}]}],sources:[{label,url}],history:[{year,programRef:null|string,status,label}],reportSummary:null|{riasec,knowledge},fitEvidence:[{groupId,category,level,z}],mappingNote}}` |
+| saveSettings | `settings,expectedRevision:int` | `settings`: `{settings,settingsRevision}` |
+| listFavorites | `cursor:null|string` | `favorites`: `{items:[{programRef,schoolName,programName,universityId,revision,updatedAtMillis}],nextCursor:null|string}` |
+| setFavorite | `programRef,value:bool,expectedRevision:int` | `favorite`: `{programRef,value,revision}` |
+
+`requestId` is also the mutation id for saveSettings/setFavorite; retries must reuse it. Conflicts return an error and never silently overwrite. Favorite removal preserves a tombstone revision. A result item always includes the favorite revision, including a removed favorite.
+
+`item` is `{programRef,year,programCode,schoolId,schoolName,programName,universityId,groupIds:[string],categories:[string],matchLevel:0|1|2,matchKind:"exact"|"extension"|"none",status:"passed"|"failed"|"pending"|"explore"|"extension",statusLabel,priorityTier:null|int,reasons:[string],missing:[string],gapSummary,favorite:bool,favoriteRevision:int}`. `universityId` may be empty for historical institutions without a current gallery match; UI disables travel in that case. Internal points are never sent.
+
+`inputs` is `{settings,report:null|{recordId,revision,selectionRevision,title},exam:null|{id,title,examDate,updatedAtMillis,summary},algorithmVersion,dataVersion}`. The report revision is the completed content revision, never a newer draft revision. All detail calls use the same captured input; detail may also inspect a valid programRef outside the current query for favorite comparison.
+
+In `details.rules`, actual/required are number or string; passed is boolean or null. Null means this rule still needs an input, with actual naming the missing input. Missing inputs never generate a fictitious zero-based boost plan or failed indicator. Exploration and pending lists may order by matchLevel (2 then 1) but keep priorityTier null; all numeric joint tiers use programRef as the sole display tiebreak.
+
+Each new query invalidates the previous query. Query snapshots expire after 30 minutes and are discarded on logout/account generation change. A stale page/detail gives `query-expired`; clients rerun query. List cursor tokens are opaque, memory-only, account-scoped and expire after 30 minutes. Pagination never fabricates omitted rows.
+
+Errors use `type:"error",code,message`. Codes: `invalid-recommendation-input`, `unavailable`, `stale-user-session`, `cloud-revision-conflict`, `mutation-id-conflict`, `not-found`, `no-active-report`, `query-expired`, `cursor-expired`, `recommendation-too-large`. A missing active report during query returns no-active-report; bootstrap still succeeds with activeReport:null. A report with no matched fit rows returns an empty exact list and warnings, never every school.
+
+Native entry: `window.StarPathHost.recommendationCommand(command)`. Web wrapper sends the ordinary account envelope `type:"recommendation-command",command`; the host emits this dedicated channel by postMessage or IPC. All replies are checked against the current request and session generation. Storage remains private under users/{uid}/recommendationSettings/main and recommendationFavorites/{year}_{code}; no changes are made to existing report, exam or university favorites.
